.Dd June 5, 2026
.Dt OCIFBSD_ORCHESTRATION 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ocifbsd_orchestration
.Nd ocifbsd pod, stack, and scheduling library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In ocifbsd/orchestration.h
.Ft int
.Fn orch_init "struct orch_config *cfg"
.Ft void
.Fn orch_shutdown "void"
.Ft int
.Fn pod_create "struct pod_spec *spec"
.Ft int
.Fn pod_start "const char *name"
.Ft int
.Fn pod_stop "const char *name" "int timeout"
.Ft int
.Fn pod_delete "const char *name"
.Ft int
.Fn pod_scale "const char *name" "int replicas"
.Ft int
.Fn stack_deploy "struct stack_spec *spec"
.Ft int
.Fn health_check_pod "const char *name"
.Ft int
.Fn rolling_update "struct pod_spec *new_spec"
.Ft int
.Fn scheduler_place "struct pod_spec *spec" "struct node_info *nodes" "int n_nodes"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library implements the high-level orchestration
primitives used by
.Xr ocifbsd 8
to manage pods, stacks, and rolling updates.
It is not a standalone program; it is linked into
the main
.Xr ocifbsd 8
binary.
.Pp
The library is organised into seven functional
modules:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Pod management
.Pq pod.c
creates, starts, stops, deletes, and scales pods
(multi-container deployment units modelled on
Kubernetes Pods).
.It
Stack management
.Pq stack.c
deploys and tears down
.Em stacks
\(em multi-pod application bundles modelled on
Docker Compose files.
.It
Scheduling
.Pq scheduler.c
selects the best node to run a pod on, based on
available CPU, memory, and resource quotas.
.It
Health checking
.Pq health.c
runs liveness and readiness probes against
running pods and reports status to the cluster.
.It
Rolling updates
.Pq rolling_update.c
performs zero-downtime updates by replacing
pod replicas one at a time.
.It
CLI plumbing
.Pq orch_cli.c
implements the
.Cm ocifbsd pod ,
.Cm ocifbsd stack ,
and
.Cm ocifbsd service
subcommand handlers.
.It
Lifecycle
.Pq orch_init.c
initialises the global orchestration state
(mutexes, trees, default config) and shuts
it down cleanly.
.El
.Pp
The library calls the container lifecycle
functions
.Pq ocifbsd_create_container , ocifbsd_start_container , etc.
that live in the main
.Xr ocifbsd 8
binary.
When the library is loaded standalone, the
.Fn stubs.c
file in this directory provides stub implementations
of those functions so the library can be linked
and tested in isolation.
When it is linked into the main
.Xr ocifbsd 8
binary, the real implementations override the stubs.
.Pp
The full public API is declared in
.In ocifbsd/orchestration.h .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/run/ocifbsd/pods -compact
.It Pa /etc/ocifbsd/orchestration.conf
Orchestration defaults (replica limits, rolling-update
parameters, health-check intervals).
.It Pa /var/run/ocifbsd/pods
Per-pod state directory.
.It Pa /var/db/ocifbsd/stacks
Stack manifests.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ocifbsd 8 ,
.Xr ocifbsd_network 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
library first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
